As we do not know that $X_ i \times _ X X_ j$ is in $\mathcal{C}$ this has to be interpreted as follows: by property (1) there exist Zariski coverings $\{ U_{ijk} \to X_ i \times _ X X_ j\} _{k \in K_{ij}}$ with $U_{ijk}$ an object of $\mathcal{C}$. Then the sheaf condition says that $F(X)$ is the equalizer of the two maps from $\prod F(X_ i)$ to $\prod F(U_{ijk})$.